00:00:21.829 --> 00:00:24.909
So I had a question about.

00:00:24.909 --> 00:00:30.800
I read an article about how Mitch McConnell
was actually trying to eliminate the six hundred

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.150
dollar per week that the people on unemployment
are receiving extra.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:36.150
Yeah.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.760
So just so people know what that is.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.730
Unemployment is a state program.

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:46.289
Different states have different levels of
unemployment benefits because of corona virus.

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:52.120
The federal government is enhancing unemployment
by up to six hundred dollars a week in addition

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.989
to what you get from the state.

00:00:53.989 --> 00:00:55.879
That's what Chris is talking about.

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:56.909
God.

00:00:56.909 --> 00:00:57.949
Right.

00:00:57.949 --> 00:01:02.640
So what do you personally believe his motivation
is behind that?

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.640
Why?

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:04.640
Why would he do that?

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:05.640
OK.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:11.170
So it's essentially a way to force states
to have to reopen.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:17.670
And if you have more and more people who are
lacking the money they need to make ends meet,

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:22.500
you are going to create a situation where
they are more likely to take the risks associated

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.840
with going back to work.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.830
I mean, it's really as simple as that.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:28.100
We we could say more about it.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.100
We could say more about.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.259
I mean, listen, I think it's short sighted
because obviously in the short term, it might

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.430
get more businesses reopened.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:38.539
If in the long term it spreads infection,
it's going to lead to more and subsequent

00:01:38.539 --> 00:01:39.539
closures.

00:01:39.539 --> 00:01:43.439
But that is what seems to be at the root of
it.

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:49.610
Yes, I believe that if it keeps going on like
this, that a lot of people are going to die.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:54.000
Yeah, we're going to have to be forced to
read it and, you know, to close again.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:02.159
I just don't I just don't understand how they
could how they could really live with themselves

00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:03.179
after doing that.

00:02:03.179 --> 00:02:05.780
So I agree with you if there is another reason.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.119
So I think that's the main reason.

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:10.830
But if there's another reason why Mitch McConnell
is doing it.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:15.280
I mean, listen, Mitch McConnell is, generally
speaking, skeptical of a lot of social welfare

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.600
programs in general.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.890
So I think any opportunity Republicans have
to cut social welfare, they will do it.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:25.500
But at least with regard to the virus, that's
that's what I think is going on for states

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.920
to open by cutting unemployment benefits.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.530
OK, well, that actually makes a little more
sense now.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:33.970
I appreciate your time, David.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:34.970
